{"slug":"forza-motorsport-4","title":"Forza Motorsport 4","desc":"Xbox 360, Turn 10 2011 (disc 1 only)","notes":["Made with the Forza importer (import_forza.py, a Blender plugin) from the game's own car archives.  Parts are the game's own names (body, bumperFa, hooda, glassLF, headlightL, interior, wheelLF ...) as children of ONE root node named like the archive; the stock car is visible.","BODY KITS (Forza Motorsport 1 / 2 / 4, Forza Horizon): every upgrade part of the shop is in the FBX, HIDDEN, at its place on the car, in Variants/<slot> (bumperF, bumperR, skirtL, skirtR, wing, hood, cage, exhaust, trunk): the game names them <part><letter>, 'a' = stock, b .. t = the tuner kits, race = the race kit.  To see them: <car>_kits.fbx = the stock car and one complete car per kit letter (the kit's parts replace the stock ones), all VISIBLE, in rows of 6.  Variants/driver = the driver mannequin (Forza 1), Variants/popup_up = pop-up lamps up.","LODs: every lower level of detail of every part (LOD2-LOD5; Forza 4 / Horizon: LOD1-LOD5 next to the LOD0 car) is HIDDEN in LODs/LOD<n>.","Left out: skeleton, locators, blur discs.  Body paint is a run time shader in all these games: one plain red (the stock paint of the first livery in Forza Motorsport), baked ambient occlusion is NOT in the FBX (it is in the plugin and in the renders).","The front of the car is +Z like in the other games; the car stands on the ground at y = 0.","Only the cars that are really on the disc dump: the dump of disc 1 has most archives as zero bytes (87 of 145) and the cars of disc 2 are not there at all.  Wheels with tyres, interior, lamps and badges are textured from the game's .xds pictures.","RIMS: the disc dump has no wheel folder (the shop wheels are on disc 2), so _Rims holds the STOCK wheel of each car that is really on the disc (57), rim and tyre as two objects.  The rim of a car file is stretched to default bounds (radius 0.194) on most cars: it is fitted to the rim of the LOD1 model (38 of the 57), which is why the rim fills its tyre, and rim and tyre are centred on the axle.  Cars with a second wheel set (wheela / wheelb) give only the first one; fer_dino246_69 has no tyre in its file."],"tags":["forza-motorsport-4"],"sections":[{"key":"cars","label":"Cars","items":[["alf_8c_08","",20028386,"forza-motorsport-4","car-alf_8c_08.zip","thumbs/forza-motorsport-4/cars/car-alf_8c_08.webp"],["ast_db5vantage_64","",19112794,"forza-motorsport-4","car-ast_db5vantage_64.zip","thumbs/forza-motorsport-4/cars/car-ast_db5vantage_64.webp"],["ast_dbr1_58","",20123880,"forza-motorsport-4","car-ast_dbr1_58.zip","thumbs/forza-motorsport-4/cars/car-ast_dbr1_58.webp"],["ast_dbs_09","",18145458,"forza-motorsport-4","car-ast_dbs_09.zip","thumbs/forza-motorsport-4/cars/car-ast_dbs_09.webp"],["ast_rapide_10","",20499866,"forza-motorsport-4","car-ast_rapide_10.zip","thumbs/forza-motorsport-4/cars/car-ast_rapide_10.webp"],["ast_v12vantage_10","",18557275,"forza-motorsport-4","car-ast_v12vantage_10.zip","thumbs/forza-motorsport-4/cars/car-ast_v12vantage_10.webp"],["aud_14_r10_10","",11407611,"forza-motorsport-4","car-aud_14_r10_10.zip","thumbs/forza-motorsport-4/cars/car-aud_14_r10_10.webp"],["aud_2_a4_11","",11210593,"forza-motorsport-4","car-aud_2_a4_11.zip","thumbs/forza-motorsport-4/cars/car-aud_2_a4_11.webp"],["aud_2_r15tdi_09","",11208598,"forza-motorsport-4","car-aud_2_r15tdi_09.zip","thumbs/forza-motorsport-4/cars/car-aud_2_r15tdi_09.webp"],["aud_2_r8_06","",9218524,"forza-motorsport-4","car-aud_2_r8_06.zip","thumbs/forza-motorsport-4/cars/car-aud_2_r8_06.webp"],["aud_8_ttr_04","",8929820,"forza-motorsport-4","car-aud_8_ttr_04.zip","thumbs/forza-motorsport-4/cars/car-aud_8_ttr_04.webp"],["ben_7_speed8_03","",10598176,"forza-motorsport-4","car-ben_7_speed8_03.zip","thumbs/forza-motorsport-4/cars/car-ben_7_speed8_03.webp"],["ben_continentalss_10","",21533993,"forza-motorsport-4","car-ben_continentalss_10.zip","thumbs/forza-motorsport-4/cars/car-ben_continentalss_10.webp"],["bm